      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled outpatient and inpatient dose of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided into a different schedule\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
